From 93201678cfb03e66c8a298aafbb94be25883a552 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caokyhieu <caokyhieu253@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:32:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(linalg,index): Kunpeng workstreams 2/5/6 - KML/KRL
 adapters, SVE/FMMLA kernels

Workstream 2 (shared FP32 centroid assignment): blocked_l2 backends selected by
LANCE_ASSIGN_BACKEND: tile (existing 4x4), f32mm (SVE FMMLA 8x4 on pair-packed
rows/centroids), kml (KML cblas_sgemm), krl / krl_ny (KRL fp32 L2 handle /
one-vs-many). All share the shortlist, exact re-score, bias and tie rules, so
ids and unbiased distances keep their contract. New F32MM CPU feature.

Workstream 5 (SUM_HACC): NEON kernel (widening adds, uzp row restore) and an
SVE1 kernel (one 32-byte TBL per plane, >= 256-bit vectors, NEON fallback);
the 920 V200 has no SVE2, so ARM previously ran the scalar kernel.

Workstream 6: SVE SUM_U16 (bit-identical to NEON); KRL FastScan bs32
candidate gated by a runtime parity check against Lance's PERM0 layout; SVE
ex_dot for 2/3/4/5/8 extra bits, bit-identical to NEON.

LANCE_KERNELS=+name,-name prefers / disables dispatch candidates so one build
benchmarks every arm. KML/KRL are compiled only with LANCE_KML_DIR /
LANCE_KRL_DIR, against the installed headers. Bench: kunpeng_kernels binary;
APPROX_MODE in the runner; new kernels recorded in manifests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
